  archivePrefix = {arXiv},
  note    = {**Read in part (abstract, Secs. 1, 2.2-2.4) on 2026-09-21; supplied by the owner from her own reading folder as `docs/reading/Euclidian Dynamical triangulation revisited 2021.pdf`.** The filename says 2021 and the title page carries a 2021 compile date, but the arXiv stamp on the PDF is 1503.03706v2, 10 June 2015 -- **verify which before citing a year.** This is the most directly useful methodological source found for T6, for five reasons. (1) **The same historical arc as ours, in a neighbouring model:** the 4D EDT transition "was long believed to be of second order until in 1996 first order behavior was found for sufficiently large systems", and this paper confirms first order up to 64k simplices. That is the finite-size argument of this project, already played out elsewhere. (2) **They beat critical slowing down with parallel tempering, not with flat-histogram sampling**, using the same swap rule `tempering.py` implements. (3) **The reason a plain chain cannot do it, stated cleanly:** at a first-order transition the correlation length stays finite, but the autocorrelation time diverges anyway because transitions between the two coexisting phases become *exponentially suppressed with increasing system size*. (4) **A warning about soft constraints:** earlier work controlled the volume with a harmonic potential, which "introduces a systematic error for all moves which change N4"; they use an infinite potential well instead. Our (S, X) window is the same kind of device and the same caution applies. They also take measurements after a fixed number of *attempted* rather than accepted moves, calling the latter a systematic error -- our sweep is already 2N attempts, so we comply. (5) **They have our ergodicity problem and say so:** "there is no set of ergodic moves known for the space of triangulations of fixed N4", so they run quasi-canonically. Useful precedent for how to report Q16 honestly. **And one thing that bears directly on T10:** they close by proposing "a class of modified path-integral measures that might remove the metastability of the Markov chain and turn the phase transition into 2nd order". A change of *measure* changing the *order* of the transition is exactly what the labelled-versus-interchangeable question asks, published, in a neighbouring model.}
}

